# Next.js 16 rules

- `params` and `searchParams` are Promises: `const { jobId } = await params;`. `cookies()` and `headers()` are async.
- Request interception lives in `src/proxy.ts` (Next 16 renamed middleware → proxy): session refresh, signed-out redirects for app routes, first-touch UTM/ref cookie. It is not the security boundary.
- Default to Server Components; `"use client"` only for interactivity. Keep client components small.
- Mutations via server actions; handle `ActionResult` (`ok` → toast/redirect; `VALIDATION` → field errors; `QUOTA_EXCEEDED`/`PRO_REQUIRED` → UpgradeModal; `CONFLICT` → info toast).
- Pages that trigger long AI actions export `maxDuration = 120`; PENDING generations are polled with `router.refresh()`.
- Route groups: (marketing) public, (auth) sign-in, (app) signed-in. App URLs: /dashboard, /library, /jobs, /contacts, /insights, /milestones, /settings, /admin.
- Use `next/font`, `next/link`, `next/image`, `notFound()`/`redirect()` from `next/navigation`, `next/og` for OG images.
